{
    "name": "VHS worn tape",
    "description": "The NES recorded and played back on a well-used NTSC SP tape in a consumer VHS deck, into a Toshiba-style slot-mask CRT. FM luma with IEC emphasis and clipping, colour-under chroma through a 1H comb, the deck's timing error and head switch. Against the measured Panasonic PV-7450 tape: 6.5 dB less carrier-to-noise, a steeper head and tape roll-off, one worn head, three times the chroma noise, four times the dropouts, and twice the timing error, on a television whose 150 Hz line loop lets the timing show. Nominal deck and tube, not a measured pair.",
